her there but besiosus is found in  five percent of ticks versus one percent  in the rest of the country says lindsay  you're just seeing as a consequence of  tick populations growing  uh into new areas that you're seeing the  emergence of these particular passages  wood has already discovered babesiosis  in ticks in ontario  and expects to soon see it in nova  scotia now he says canada needs more  testing to keep track of the trends  my hope is that we'll have better  treatment  for his disease and the ones to come  jimmy morocco global news toronto  now recycle more next the pressure on g7  leaders to deal with electronic waste  this was a case of swift justice on  tuesday  a man slapped french president emmanuel  macron in the face  today that man was sentenced to four  months in jail the 28 year old claims he  didn't plan to slap  mackerel but says he was filled with  disgust when he saw the president  face to face well macron's face along  with the other g7 leaders are staring  back at them from across the water at  the g7 summit in cornwall  a massive mount rushmore style sculpture  has been created with scraps of  electronic waste  it was commissioned by a british  retailer that sells second-hand  electronics but it does have a political  message  crystal demancing reports  it's a twist on the mounting issue of  electronic waste  and all eyes are now on those who can do  something about it  let's try and build things that we can  repair let's build things that last  longer let's  you know not have to have the new newest  thing every time but  you know let's find a way to dealing  with this before we just get buried  under it  mount recyclemore like many of joe  rush's creations is born of his  environmental and anti-consumerism  beliefs  e-waste may not be top of mind for most  but it has a  huge impact those who work in the world  of recycled electronics  want people to see its weight it's 53  million tons of  of e-waste that's created every year of  which t